        <body>
            <div xml:id="d334">

                <pb facs="0378" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg344"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mills to Mr. Olney.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1897-01-06"><hi rendition="#italic">January
                                6, 1897</hi></date>. (Received Jan. 21.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 179.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It is with deep regret that I have to
                    inform you of the death of Mr. Albert S. Willis, envoy extraordinary and
                    minister plenipotentiary of the United States, which occurred this morning at
                    8.30.</p>
                <p>The funeral services will take place on the 8th instant, after which the remains
                    will be placed in a vault until the 13th instant, when they will be shipped to
                    San Francisco, on the steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Australia</hi>, en route
                    to Louisville, Ky., the home of the late minister.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ellis Mills</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
